<task id="006" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-record access, hide-don't-disable, "Your access" — remove both ViewOnly hard-codes (FR-06, FR-07)</title>
    <phase>1 Record template and actions</phase>
    <gate>after 002 and 004</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-driven UI behaviour across .ts/.tsx files (tags frontend, authorization, integration-test)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization behaviour with a hard invariant: no action the UI offers may answer 403</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Sequential chain on the template files (003 → 005 → 004 → 006 → 007); also touches SmartTodo/EventsCalendar shared with 004</parallel-reason>
    <deps>002, 004</deps>
    <tags>frontend, react, authorization, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>5-7 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Drive Upload, New message, Add to-do, Add event and delete-own on every record from the server's per-record answer (`/me` `writeAccessPerRecord` and each list's `canCreate`), remove both ViewOnly hard-codes and the project-only create gates, hide (never disable) what the caller cannot do, add one "why" line per read-only section, and show "Your access" in the record header.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in React and external-plane authorization semantics (ADR-028 A1, ADR-003 fail closed). Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>On matters, projects and work assignments a caller with Create sees and can use all four actions and a View-only caller sees none (no disabled placeholders); every offered action's POST is the one task 002 proved answers 201 for that caller; the header names the caller's right; tests prove both access levels on matter and work assignment to-dos and events.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-06, FR-07, NFR-04; project gotcha 2026-11-09 (two hard-codes). Hard-codes verified 2026-11-10: the template's Tasks &amp; events section passes `AccessLevel.ViewOnly` (moved by task 005 from `RecordDetailModal.tsx:524-525`); `SmartTodo.tsx:629` forces ViewOnly for non-project roots, and `:655`/`:659` keep create/toggle project-only. A third, unlisted gate: `EventsCalendar.tsx:588-592` allows create only when `root === 'projects'`. The SPA create clients are project-only: `createEvent` (`web-api-client.ts:721-729`) and `createTodo` (`:796-798`). Task 002 adds the matter/WA event routes and makes the to-do, event and message lists return `canCreate` to every caller; `DocumentLibrary` already follows its list's `canCreate` (`DocumentLibrary.tsx:701`, `:748-766`). `/me` carries levels for projects only (`bff-client.ts:145-176`).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/SmartTodo.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/EventsCalendar.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/detail/RecordMessages.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/api/web-api-client.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/RecordTemplateModal.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/sections/TasksEventsSection.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/sections/DocumentsSection.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/sections/MessagesSection.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/src/components/record/recordAccess.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/external-spa/tests/RecordTemplateAccess.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/tests/PerRecordWriteAccess.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/tests/DetailEventsTodosRoots.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/components/DocumentLibrary.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/src/auth/bff-client.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/tests/ProjectPage.perRecordWrite.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalRootEventCreateContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="002" status="pending">Matter/WA event POST routes; list `canCreate` for every caller on to-dos, events and messages</dependency>
      <dependency task="004" status="pending">Toolbar actions open in-parent dialogs</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-06 / NFR-04">Each of the four create actions on a record is shown only when that record's matching list answered `canCreate === true` (documents → Upload, messages → New message, to-dos → Add to-do, events → Add event). Absent, null, a failed list read or a still-loading list = hidden. The one exception kept: a project for a caller without `writeAccessPerRecord` may still use its `/me` level where its list sends no `canCreate` (today's ProjectPage rule), and must agree with the list when both exist.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-06">Remove `AccessLevel.ViewOnly` from the Tasks &amp; events section, the `root === 'projects'` force at `SmartTodo.tsx:629` and the project-only conditions at `SmartTodo.tsx:655/659` and `EventsCalendar.tsx:588-592`. Creates call root-aware clients (`createRootTodo(root, id, …)`, `createRootEvent(root, id, …)`) built on the existing `rootTodosPath`/`rootEventsPath` (`web-api-client.ts:534-539`); the project wrappers stay as thin calls to them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-06">The to-do status toggle on a matter or work assignment is shown only when the caller's right to PATCH that to-do is known from a server answer; if none is available it stays hidden there (never offered to fail).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-07">A caller without write sees only Refresh, Copy link and Download (where the type has it). No disabled create control appears anywhere in the template. Delete-own stays driven by the creator stamp, unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-07">Each read-only section shows exactly one short line saying why (e.g. Messages: "You can read this thread. Posting needs Collaborate access."). All lines and the header labels live in one map in `recordAccess.ts`; a caller with `writeAccessPerRecord` gets wording that does not name a grant level.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-07">The header's "Your access" value is derived only from what the BFF answered for this record: a project's `/me` level label, otherwise "Can contribute" when any of the record's lists answered `canCreate: true` and "Read only" when all answered false. Unknown (lists not loaded) shows nothing rather than a guess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A1">The client decides only what is shown; it never sends a level and never skips the server's check. A 403 from any action still shows the existing error and changes nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`ProjectPage` behaviour is unchanged except that it inherits the root-aware clients; its tests pass unchanged.</constraint>
  </constraints>

