  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Add the root-aware create clients; repoint the project wrappers.</step>
    <step order="2">Remove the hard-codes and project-only gates in SmartTodo, EventsCalendar and the Tasks &amp; events section; apply the list-`canCreate` rule.</step>
    <step order="3">Read `canCreate` from the message list (task 002) in RecordMessages; hide the inline compose when it is not true and show the read-only line.</step>
    <step order="4">Write `recordAccess.ts` (rights per record from the list answers + `/me`; texts map) and feed the toolbar visibility and the header "Your access" line from it.</step>
    <step order="5">Write `tests/RecordTemplateAccess.test.tsx` with mocked BFF responses: for matter and for work assignment, Create holder vs View-only, for to-dos and events (plus documents and messages); update `PerRecordWriteAccess.test.tsx` and `DetailEventsTodosRoots.test.tsx`.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm run lint` and `npm test` in `src/client/external-spa`; confirm task 002's contract tests (`ExternalRootEventCreateContractTests`, the list `canCreate` tests) pass on this branch.</step>
    <step order="7">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations and decisions in `projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-006-notes.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any of the four actions has no server `canCreate` for some root or caller kind after task 002, STOP: do not infer it from another list; a new server answer is a UAC-reviewed BFF change (new task).</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner expects a named grant level ("View only / Collaborate / Full access") in "Your access" for matters, work assignments, invoices or service requests, STOP: `/me` carries levels for projects only, so that needs a BFF change.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`DocumentLibrary.tsx:748-766` already derives Upload from its list's `canCreate`; `useAccessLevel.ts` (`canUpload`, `mapAccessLevelString`) maps `/me` project levels; `rootTodosPath`/`rootEventsPath` (`web-api-client.ts:534-539`) already build root routes for reads.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the clients and the per-section rules (extended in place). `recordAccess.ts` is new only because the record-level aggregate (toolbar visibility across four lists, the header "Your access" value and the read-only texts) has no existing home; it reuses `useAccessLevel` for project labels.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Matter and work-assignment to-dos and events stay read-only for callers who hold Create, and the header cannot name the caller's right (FR-06, FR-07 acceptance fail).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Write caller sees and uses all four actions">
      <url>{spa-dev-url}/?record=matter:{matter-id-collaborate}</url>
      <steps><step>Sign in as a partner with Collaborate on the matter; open it.</step><step>Use Upload, New message, Add to-do and Add event once each.</step><step>Repeat on a work assignment and a project.</step></steps>
      <expected>All four actions are visible and each succeeds (no 403); "Your access" names the right.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="View-only caller sees none">
      <url>{spa-dev-url}/?record=matter:{matter-id-viewonly}</url>
      <steps><step>Sign in as a View-only partner; open the matter, a work assignment and a project.</step><step>Inspect toolbar and sections.</step></steps>
      <expected>Only Refresh and Copy link; no disabled buttons; each read-only section shows its one-line reason; "Your access" says Read only.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps><step>Repeat the View-only test in dark theme.</step></steps>
      <expected>The access lines and header use semantic tokens.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">typecheck, lint and vitest in src/client/external-spa</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Run task 002's contract tests to confirm the server side</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

