  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a matter, a project and a work assignment whose lists answer `canCreate: true`, all four actions are visible and each submits to the record's own root route (to-dos/events to `/{root}/{id}/…`).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given lists that answer `canCreate: false`, none of the four actions is in the DOM, no disabled placeholder exists, and each read-only section shows its one line.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a list that fails, is loading, or omits `canCreate`, its action is hidden (fail closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No action the UI offers answers 403: for matter and work-assignment to-dos and events, the SPA tests' visibility table equals the 201/403 table of task 002's contract tests (cited by test name in the task notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A grep of `src/client/external-spa/src` finds no `AccessLevel.ViewOnly` passed as a prop and no `root === 'projects'` create/toggle gate in SmartTodo or EventsCalendar.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">"Your access" shows the project level label, "Can contribute" or "Read only" per the FR-07 constraint, and nothing while unknown; the text for each access level is asserted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Delete-own still shows only on the caller's own rows; a 403 from any action shows the existing error and the list is unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ProjectPage tests (`ProjectPage.perRecordWrite.test.tsx` and others) pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">typecheck, lint and the vitest suite pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract (both access levels × matter/work assignment × to-dos/events, plus documents and messages visibility, the fail-closed cases and the header text). Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-06, FR-07, NFR-04; spec §Affected Areas lists only the two hard-codes — the `EventsCalendar.tsx:588-592` gate and the project-only create clients were found on 2026-11-10 and are in scope here because FR-06 cannot be met without them. Two adversarial-review passes (authorization).

